{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.genus_from_hecke_completeness","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Archimedean.genus_from_hecke_completeness","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Order.Interval.Finset.Nat","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Finset.Prod","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Finset.Card","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Nat.GCD.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.IntervalCases"],"declarations":8,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.blockRankBound_at_four_lt_five","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.blockRankBound_at_four_lt_five","kind":"theorem","line":92,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/genus_from_hecke_completeness.lean#L92-L103","doc":"**The block bound at `g = 4` is four, so the spanning criterion fails.**\n\nRank is additive over the blocks of a block-diagonal matrix and each block\nis capped by the smaller of its dimensions, so the rank of the character\nmatrix is at most `min r₂ 2 + min r₃ 3` where `rᵢ` is the number of\n`i`-strand rows.  Derived from the two counts above rather than asserted:\n`min 4 2 + min 2 3 = 2 + 2 = 4`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.strandCountThree_at_four","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.strandCountThree_at_four","kind":"theorem","line":86,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/genus_from_hecke_completeness.lean#L86-L90","doc":"Only **two** of the six are three-strand closures — and that is what\ncaps the rank, since the `H₃(q)` block has three columns to fill. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.strandCountTwo_at_four","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.strandCountTwo_at_four","kind":"theorem","line":81,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/genus_from_hecke_completeness.lean#L81-L84","doc":"Four of the six rows at `g = 4` are two-strand closures. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.genus_from_hecke_completeness","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.genus_from_hecke_completeness","kind":"theorem","line":68,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/genus_from_hecke_completeness.lean#L68-L79","doc":"**`g = 4` is the least genus at which the count reaches five.**\n\nThis is the half of `lem:genus-from-hecke-completeness` that is true.\nStated as an inequality, because the count at `g = 4` is 6; an earlier\nversion stated `= 5` and understated the count to match. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:lem:genus-from-hecke-completeness","label":"lem:genus-from-hecke-completeness","md":"quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/genus-from-hecke-completeness.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.torusKnotEmbeddingCount_four","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.torusKnotEmbeddingCount_four","kind":"theorem","line":63,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/genus_from_hecke_completeness.lean#L63-L66","doc":"The count at `g = 4` is **six**, not five: `T_{2,3}, T_{2,5}, T_{2,7},\nT_{2,9}` from `r = 2` and `T_{3,4}, T_{3,5}` from `r = 3`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.torusKnotEmbeddingCount","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.torusKnotEmbeddingCount","kind":"def","line":60,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/genus_from_hecke_completeness.lean#L60-L61","doc":"`N g`, the count of those knots. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.embeddableTorusKnots","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.embeddableTorusKnots","kind":"def","line":53,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/genus_from_hecke_completeness.lean#L53-L58","doc":"The torus knots `T_{r,s}` with `r ∈ {2, 3}`, `r < s`, `gcd r s = 1`, of\nSeifert genus at most `g`.  The column bound `2g + 2` is safe: genus at\nmost `g` forces `s ≤ 2g + 1` when `r = 2` and `s ≤ g + 1` when `r = 3`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.torusKnotGenus","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.torusKnotGenus","kind":"def","line":49,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/genus_from_hecke_completeness.lean#L49-L51","doc":"Seifert genus of the torus knot `T_{r,s}` for coprime `r < s`:\n`(r-1)(s-1)/2`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}